{"id":4033,"date":"2023-12-05T10:35:45","date_gmt":"2023-12-05T10:35:45","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/?p=4033"},"modified":"2024-12-10T12:23:16","modified_gmt":"2024-12-10T12:23:16","slug":"springfield-children-present-their-concepts-for-a-climate-changed-future","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/springfield-children-present-their-concepts-for-a-climate-changed-future\/","title":{"rendered":"Springfield children present their concepts for a climate changed future"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-text stk-block-text stk-block stk-2b67d6e\" data-block-id=\"2b67d6e\"><p class=\"stk-block-text__text\"><em><br><\/em><\/p><\/div>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"2472\" height=\"2080\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/IMG_2746-edit-3.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-4040 lazyload\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/IMG_2746-edit-3.jpg 2472w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/IMG_2746-edit-3-300x252.jpg 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/IMG_2746-edit-3-1024x862.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/IMG_2746-edit-3-768x646.jpg 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/IMG_2746-edit-3-1536x1292.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/IMG_2746-edit-3-2048x1723.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/IMG_2746-edit-3-238x200.jpg 238w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/IMG_2746-edit-3-149x125.jpg 149w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 2472px) 100vw, 2472px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 2472px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 2472\/2080;\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>On Friday 1 December, the CCAC review panel visited Springfield Primary School in Sale, Manchester for the next stage of our co-design project on sustainable living. <\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Ninety Year 5 children presented ideas for their homes and neighbourhoods in the year 2050.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They were asked to conceive the buildings and settings in three climate extremes \u2013 very hot, very cold, or flooded &#8211; whilst also meeting net zero carbon criteria, social and regenerative precepts.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"2016\" height=\"1512\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/panel.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-4035 lazyload\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/panel.jpg 2016w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/panel-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/panel-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/panel-768x576.jpg 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/panel-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/panel-267x200.jpg 267w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/12\/panel-167x125.jpg 167w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 2016px) 100vw, 2016px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 2016px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 2016\/1512;\" \/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"><em>The CCAC review panel before the presentations<\/em><\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The expert review panel was amazed and delighted at the imagination of the children\u2019s designs and their grasp of climate change issues. Several groups performed their presentations to get their ideas across, and another composed a poem to capture the zeitgeist.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Congratulations&nbsp;to Springfield pupils, teachers, and the designers from Levitt Bernstein Architects for embracing both climate science and design creativity to enhance learning.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>On Friday 1 December, the CCAC review panel were presented with our Springfield children&#8217;s designs<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":4044,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[12],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-4033","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-ccac-news"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.5 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/product\/yoast-seo-wordpress\/ -->\n<title>Springfield children present their concepts for a climate changed future - Climate Change All Change<\/title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/springfield-children-present-their-concepts-for-a-climate-changed-future\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_GB\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Springfield children present their concepts for a climate changed future - Climate Change All Change\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"On Friday 1 December, the CCAC review panel were presented with our Springfield children&#039;s designs\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/springfield-children-present-their-concepts-for-a-climate-changed-future\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Climate Change All Change\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2023-12-05T10:35:45+00:00\" \/>\n<meta pr